<title>EGYPT: Yield dips on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield dips on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.115 percent from 10.121 percent at the previous auction on December 9.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: June 17, 1997 (June 10, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.115 percent (10.121)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 927.625 million (970.550 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.081 billion (1.119 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.999-10.136 percent (9.999-10.149)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.999-10.200 percent (9.999-10.400)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 93 (108)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 107 (131)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 Egyptian pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
